{"files":[{"content":"#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <math.h>\n\nstatic void bubble_sort(double *values, int count) {\n    int i, j;\n    double temporary;\n\n    for (i = count - 1; i > 0; i--) {\n        for (j = 0; j < i; j++) {\n            if (values[j] > values[j + 1]) {\n                temporary = values[j];\n                values[j] = values[j + 1];\n                values[j + 1] = temporary;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nstatic void stable_merge_sort(double *values, double *scratch, size_t count) {\n    double *source = values;\n    double *destination = scratch;\n    size_t width = 1;\n\n    while (width < count) {\n        size_t start = 0;\n\n        while (start < count) {\n            size_t middle = width > count - start ? count : start + width;\n            size_t end = width > count - middle ? count : middle + width;\n            size_t left = start;\n            size_t right = middle;\n            size_t output = start;\n\n            while (left < middle && right < end) {\n                if (source[left] <= source[right]) {\n                    destination[output++] = source[left++];\n                } else {\n                    destination[output++] = source[right++];\n                }\n            }\n            while (left < middle) {\n                destination[output++] = source[left++];\n            }\n            while (right < end) {\n                destination[output++] = source[right++];\n            }\n            start = end;\n        }\n\n        {\n            double *temporary = source;\n            source = destination;\n            destination = temporary;\n        }\n\n        if (width > count / 2) {\n            break;\n        }\n        width *= 2;\n    }\n\n    if (source != values) {\n        size_t i;\n        for (i = 0; i < count; i++) {\n            values[i] = source[i];\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nstatic void ordena_colunas(double *matriz, int lin, int col) {\n    int i, j;\n    double *scratch = (double *)malloc((size_t)lin * sizeof(double));\n\n    for (i = 0; i < col; i++) {\n        double *values = matriz + (size_t)i * (size_t)lin;\n        int contains_nan = 0;\n\n        for (j = 0; j < lin; j++) {\n            if (isnan(values[j])) {\n                contains_nan = 1;\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n\n        if (contains_nan || scratch == NULL) {\n            bubble_sort(values, lin);\n        } else {\n            stable_merge_sort(values, scratch, (size_t)lin);\n        }\n    }\n\n    free(scratch);\n}\n\nstatic void calcula_mediana(const double * restrict matriz,\n                            double * restrict vet, int lin, int col) {\n    int i;\n\n    if ((lin - 1) % 2) {\n#pragma GCC ivdep\n        for (i = 0; i < col; i++) {\n            size_t base = (size_t)i * (size_t)lin;\n            vet[i] = matriz[base + (size_t)(lin / 2 - 1)] +\n                     matriz[base + (size_t)(lin / 2)];\n            vet[i] *= 0.5;\n        }\n    } else {\n#pragma GCC ivdep\n        for (i = 0; i < col; i++) {\n            size_t base = (size_t)i * (size_t)lin;\n            vet[i] = matriz[base + (size_t)(lin / 2)];\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nstatic double moda_aux(const double *matriz, int lin) {\n    int i;\n    float conta = 0.0f;\n    float moda = 0.0f;\n\n    if (lin < 2) {\n        return -1;\n    }\n\n    /* Preserve pairwise comparison behavior when NaNs disrupt sorted runs. */\n    for (i = 0; i < lin; i++) {\n        if (isnan(matriz[i])) {\n            int j;\n            for (i = 0; i < lin; i++) {\n                double cont = 0.0;\n                for (j = i + 1; j < lin; j++) {\n                    if (matriz[i] == matriz[j]) {\n                        cont++;\n                        if (cont > conta) {\n                            conta = (float)cont;\n                            moda = (float)matriz[i];\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            return conta == 0.0f ? -1 : moda;\n        }\n    }\n\n    {\n        int run_length = 1;\n        double run_value = matriz[0];\n\n        for (i = 1; i < lin; i++) {\n            if (matriz[i] == matriz[i - 1]) {\n                run_length++;\n                if ((double)(run_length - 1) > conta) {\n                    conta = (float)(run_length - 1);\n                    moda = (float)run_value;\n                }\n            } else {\n                run_length = 1;\n                run_value = matriz[i];\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    return conta == 0.0f ? -1 : moda;\n}\n\nstatic void calcula_moda(const double *matriz, double *moda, int lin, int col) {\n    int i;\n    for (i = 0; i < col; i++) {\n        moda[i] = moda_aux(matriz + (size_t)i * (size_t)lin, lin);\n    }\n}\n\nstatic void calcula_variancia(const double *matriz, const double *media,\n                              double *variancia, int lin, int col) {\n    int i, j;\n    for (i = 0; i < col; i++) {\n        double soma = 0.0;\n        size_t base = (size_t)i * (size_t)lin;\n        for (j = 0; j < lin; j++) {\n            double diferenca = matriz[base + (size_t)j] - media[i];\n            soma += pow(diferenca, 2);\n        }\n        variancia[i] = soma / (lin - 1);\n    }\n}\n\nstatic void calcula_desvio_padrao(const double * restrict variancia,\n                                  double * restrict dp, int col) {\n    int i;\n#pragma GCC ivdep\n    for (i = 0; i < col; i++) {\n        dp[i] = sqrt(variancia[i]);\n    }\n}\n\nstatic void calcula_coeficiente_variacao(const double * restrict media,\n                                         const double * restrict dp,\n                                         double * restrict cv, int col) {\n    int i;\n#pragma GCC ivdep\n    for (i = 0; i < col; i++) {\n        cv[i] = dp[i] / media[i];\n    }\n}\n\nint main(void) {\n    int lin, col, i, j;\n    double *matriz, *mediana, *media, *media_har, *moda;\n    double *variancia, *dp, *cv;\n\n    fscanf(stdin, \"%d \", &lin);\n    fscanf(stdin, \"%d\\n\", &col);\n\n    matriz = (double *)malloc((size_t)lin * (size_t)col * sizeof(double));\n    media = (double *)malloc((size_t)col * sizeof(double));\n    media_har = (double *)malloc((size_t)col * sizeof(double));\n    mediana = (double *)malloc((size_t)col * sizeof(double));\n    moda = (double *)malloc((size_t)col * sizeof(double));\n    variancia = (double *)malloc((size_t)col * sizeof(double));\n    cv = (double *)malloc((size_t)col * sizeof(double));\n    dp = (double *)malloc((size_t)col * sizeof(double));\n\n    for (j = 0; j < col; j++) {\n        media[j] = 0.0;\n        media_har[j] = 0.0;\n    }\n\n    for (i = 0; i < lin; i++) {\n        for (j = 0; j < col; j++) {\n            size_t index = (size_t)j * (size_t)lin + (size_t)i;\n            double valor;\n            fscanf(stdin, \"%lf \", &valor);\n            matriz[index] = valor;\n            media[j] += valor;\n            media_har[j] += 1 / valor;\n        }\n    }\n\n    for (j = 0; j < col; j++) {\n        media[j] /= lin;\n        media_har[j] = lin / media_har[j];\n    }\n\n    ordena_colunas(matriz, lin, col);\n    calcula_mediana(matriz, mediana, lin, col);\n    calcula_moda(matriz, moda, lin, col);\n    calcula_variancia(matriz, media, variancia, lin, col);\n    calcula_desvio_padrao(variancia, dp, col);\n    calcula_coeficiente_variacao(media, dp, cv, col);\n\n    for (i = 0; i < col; i++)\n        printf(\"%.1lf \", media[i]);\n    printf(\"\\n\");\n    for (i = 0; i < col; i++)\n        printf(\"%.1lf \", media_har[i]);\n    printf(\"\\n\");\n    for (i = 0; i < col; i++)\n        printf(\"%.1lf \", mediana[i]);\n    printf(\"\\n\");\n    for (i = 0; i < col; i++)\n        printf(\"%.1lf \", moda[i]);\n    printf(\"\\n\");\n    for (i = 0; i < col; i++)\n        printf(\"%.1lf \", variancia[i]);\n    printf(\"\\n\");\n    for (i = 0; i < col; i++)\n        printf(\"%.1lf \", dp[i]);\n    printf(\"\\n\");\n    for (i = 0; i < col; i++)\n        printf(\"%.1lf \", cv[i]);\n    printf(\"\\n\");\n\n    free(matriz);\n    free(media);\n    free(media_har);\n    free(mediana);\n    free(moda);\n    free(variancia);\n    free(dp);\n    free(cv);\n    return 0;\n}\n","path":"src/est_matriz_seq.c"}],"hypothesis":"Replacing quadratic bubble sorting with a stable O(n log n) merge sort for NaN-free columns should reduce sorting cost without changing sorted order or metric results. Combining this with archived input-time mean accumulation, sorted-run mode counting, and independent-loop vectorization may improve the full program; NaN-containing columns retain the original bubble-sort ordering.","notes":"One bounded source experiment only; no commands were run. Stable merging preserves the original order of equal values, and columns containing NaNs use bubble sort to preserve its comparison behavior. The controller should evaluate full-program correctness and performance.","research":{"queries":[],"urls":[]},"sources_kept":["fa0655c581fd428e"],"transformations":["Use stable bottom-up merge sort for NaN-free columns, with a reusable temporary buffer; retain bubble sort for columns containing NaNs or if buffer allocation fails.","Accumulate arithmetic and harmonic sums as each value is read, then normalize once per column.","Replace allocated pairwise mode counting for sorted non-NaN columns with a linear equal-value run scan, preserving float mode/count behavior; retain pairwise counting for columns containing NaNs.","Retain restrict-qualified pointers and GCC ivdep hints on independent median, standard-deviation, and coefficient-of-variation loops."]}